I initially have given up to work on this problem at this point and only resumed later --- and as I reflected on it, most of my strategies have been to force the faces to be  $``\text{somehow even}"$  vertice-wise, or to induct downward edge-wise. I looked for another path this time, and that initially was to connect adjacent faces with an auxiliary edge. This doesn't add or simplify any complex structure to the problem, so I resolved to consider edge first, face later instead of face first, edge later. 
Keeping the  $``\text{background mindset}"$  intact, I proceeded to randomly colour 2 edges (following the idea in **Section 2**) instead of 1, and a nice picture emerged! (Since all faces needed to have a sum of 0, summing through it all, it would make sense to only make the edges with numbers +1/-1 --- and, the two edges I colored was part of the bottom-right 5-cycle) 
