ambda-bc}|=|\frac{bm-an+\lambda}{(a^2+b^2)\lambda}|=|\frac{am+bn+c}{(a^2+b^2)c}|=\frac{k}{ab} $$  Now just check that   $$ m=\frac{n(ac+b\lambda)}{bc-a\lambda} $$    works. So for any  $n$  we have an  $m$  . Hence atleast one point exists. Done. (we have a condition  $n \neq 0$  )  $\blacksquare$ .

