First, note that cliques will always stay the same under the operation  $(').$  Define a maximal cycle as a cycle  $S \in G,$  such that there doesn't exist a cycle  $C \in G$  such that  $S \subset C.$  Also, WLOG  $G$  is connected (otherwise we can split into its connected components). Note that a clique in  $G$  will always be a clique in  $G.$ **Lemma 1:** A maximal cycle cannot be connected by an edge to a vertex (or multiple vertices)
