<span style="color:#f00">**Claim:**</span>  $B_1C_2$  is tangent to circumcircle of  $ABC$  at  $H_A.$ <span style="color:#00f">**Proof:**</span> We will complex bash. Toss  $ABC$  onto the unit circle with coordinates  $a, b, c.$ We have  $H = a + b + c, D = \frac12(b + c + a - bc\overline{a}).$  Thus,  $H_A = -\frac{bc}{a}.$  Hence, if  $C_2’$  is  $H_AH_A\cap BB,$  we have  $C_2’ = \frac{-2\frac{bc}{a}\cdot b}{b - \frac{bc}a} = \frac{2bc}{c - a}.$  We also know  $N$  is  $\frac{a + b + c}{2}$  by its definition. However, 
\begin{align*}
\frac{\frac{a + b + c}{2} - c}{a + b + c + \frac{2bc}{c - a}}& = \frac{\frac{a + b - c}{2}}{a + b + c + \frac{2bc}{c - a}} 
& = \frac12\frac{(a + b - c)(c - a)}{c^2 - a^2 + bc - ba - 2bc} 
& = \frac12\frac{(a + b - c)(c - a)}{c^2 - a^2 - bc - ba}  
& = \frac12 \frac{(a + b - c)(c - a)}{(c - a - b)(a + c)} 
& = -\frac12 \frac{a - c}{a + c}
\end{align*}
but
\begin{align*}
\overline{\frac{a - c}{a + c}} & = \frac{c - a}{a + c}
\end{align*} 
which implies our claim.

