Combining the two results, we get there is an involution swapping   $$  (S,S),(C,D),(K_1,K_0),)(L_1,L_0)  $$  Let  $T$  be a point on  $\ell$  such that  $\ell$  bisects  $\angle DTC$ . The reflection in  $\ell$  swaps  $(S,S)$  and  $(C,D)$ , so it must swap  $(K_1,K_0)$  and  $(L_1,L_0)$  also. Hence we get   $$  \ell \text{ bisects } \angle K_0TK_1 , \angle L_0TL_1 $$  As  $K,L$  are reflection of  $K_0,L_0$  in  $\ell$ , we get   $$  T \in KK_1,LL_1 $$  Hence lines  $AK,BL$  concur at  $T$ , which completes the proof.  $\blacksquare$

