Define  $P=AK\cap IJ$  and  $X$  be the exsimilicenter of  $\omega_A$  and  $\omega_B$ . Also let  $E$  and  $F$  denote the tangencies of  $\omega_A$  and  $\omega_B$  with  $CD$  respectively.

Firstly, from 2 points DDIT on  $\omega_B$  with the tangency points  $F$  and  $L$  w.r.t.  $B$  gives that  $(BX,BX)$ ,  $(BL,BF)$  and  $(BC,BD)$  swap under some Involution. Projecting this Involution onto  $CD$ , we get that there exists an Involution on  $CD$  swapping  $(X,X)$ ,  $(BL\cap CD,F)$  and  $(C,D)$ . Similarly, by another 2 points DDIT on  $\omega_A$  with tangency points  $K$  and  $E$  w.r.t.  $A$ , and then projecting that Involution onto  $CD$ , we get that  $(X,X)$ ,  $(AK\cap CD,E)$  and  $(C,D)$  swap under some Involution. However, we previously got that  $(X,X)$  and  $(C,D)$  were also getting swapped, so this must mean that both the Involutions are the same.

Now thus, we have an Involution on  $CD$  swapping  $(X,X)$ ,  $(C,D)$ ,  $(BL\cap CD,F)$  and  $(AK\cap CD,E)$ . Now un-projecting this Involution from  $P$ , we get that  $(PX,PX)$ ,  $(PC,PD)$ ,  $(P(BL\cap CD),PF)$  and  $(PA,PE)$  swap under some Involution  $\Phi$  on the pencil of lines through  $P$ .

Now finally note that the map  $\Psi$  on the pencil of lines through  $P$  by performing a reflection over line  $PX$  is an Involution. Now moreover as  $P$  lies on the line joining the centers of  $\omega_A$  and  $\omega_B$ , we get that  $PK$  and  $PE$  swap under this Involution  $\Psi$ . And also, clearly the line  $PX$  is invariant under  $\Psi$ , so  $\Psi$  swaps  $(PX,PX)$  and  $(PA,PE)$  but previously we had that  $\Phi$  also swapped the same pairs, which forces both these Involutions to be the same!

Thus we get that our map  $\Phi$  was basically the reflection of the pencil of lines through  $P$  over  $PX$ . This means that  $P(BL\cap CD)$  and  $PF$  are reflections over  $PX$ . Now analogously we also have  $PL$  and  $PF$  are reflections over  $PX$ , which finally means that  $P(BL\cap CD)\equiv PL$  which simply means that  $\overline{P-L-B}$  are collinear and we are done! :stretcher:

