Firstly, observe that
\begin{align*}
    \angle{FAD} &= \angle{BAD} 
    &= 180^\circ - \angle{BCD} 
    &= 180^\circ - \angle{FED},
\end{align*}
so it follows that  $AFED$  is cyclic. 

Hence, we have
\begin{align*}
    2\angle{FBD} &= 2\angle{ABD} 
    &= 2\angle{ACD} 
    &= 2(90^\circ-\angle{BEC}) 
    &= 180^\circ - 2\angle{BEC} 
    &= 180^\circ - \angle{AEC} 
    &= \angle{AED} 
    &= \angle{AFD} 
    &= 180^\circ-\angle{BFD}.
\end{align*}
This implies that  $FB=FD,$  so we are done.  $\square$

