Let \(X=\overline{AE}\cap\overline{BC}\). Since \(\triangle ABX\sim\triangle CEX\) we may select \(t\) such that \(BX=3t\) and \(EX=7t\). Then the area of the parallelogram is both \(CX\cdot AB=3(11-3t)\) and \(AX\cdot CE=7(9-7t)\). Setting these equal, \begin{align*}     3(11-3t)&=7(9-7t)     \implies 40t&=30\implies t=3/4. \end{align*}
It follows that the area of the parallelogram is \(3(11-3t)=105/4\), and the requested sum is \(105+4=109\).

