\[\angle OGY + \angle OMY = 90^\circ+90^\circ = 180^\circ.\]

Hence,  $OGYM$  is also a cyclic quadrilateral meaning

\[\angle GOY = \angle GMY \equiv \angle AMZ.\]

Thus, we have

\begin{align*}
\angle XOY &= \angle GOX + \angle GOY 
&= \angle MAZ + \angle AMZ 
&= 180^\circ - \angle AZM 
&= 180^\circ - (\angle ABY-\angle ZAB) 
&= 180^\circ - \angle B + \angle C.
\end{align*}

Substituing our values in, we see that

\[17x=180-13x+2x \equiv x = \frac{45}{7}\]

The answer is thus  $\frac{585}{7} \implies \boxed{592}$ .

