Let  $d = \frac{30}{abc}$ . Plugging this into the third equation gives \[abc + 30\left(\frac{ab+ bc+ca}{abc} \right) = 14 \] Now plugging in  $ab + bc + ca = -4$  we get a quadratic in  $abc$ . Solving we have either  $abc = 20$  or  $abc = -6$ . Checking  $abc = -6$  fails so we take  $abc = 20$ . Thus  $d = \frac{3}{2}$ . Then we have the system,
